          "page": 1,
          "section": "abstract",
          "quote": "Microcrack suppression is a challenging issue in additive manufacturing of tungsten heavy alloys (WHAs) due to the high melting point and brittleness of tungsten (W). In this study, W-5Nb samples with a high density and few defects were successfully manufactured by introducing niobium (Nb) using selective laser melting (SLM) technique",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
